# Bastion Pass Release Notes

## 1.0.0 (16 May 2026)
* Update README.md file
* Rename PyPass to Bastion Pass
* Update Buy me a Coffee link to new username
* Fix background server so user can now login

## 1.0.0 (06 June 2026)
* Started fixing migration server

## 1.0.0 (07 June 2026)
* Set up framework for data migration into background server

## 1.0.0 (12 June 2026)
* Start adding sending data functionality into background server
* Simplify add_to_screen function
* Temporarily disable backup phrase creation

## 1.0.0 (04 July 2026)
* Fix server event loop being blocked, triggering constant warning in console

## 1.0.0 (08 July 2026)
* Replaced httpx and debug server with message listener inside of app
* Fix background server so app can start it on startup, and doesn't block app thread

## 1.0.0 (09 July 2026)
* Layout most of the UI for importing passwords from files
* Start working on the import passwords from files functionality

## 1.0.0 (10 July 2026)
* Work on functionality for importing passwords from files

## 1.0.0 (11 July 2026)
* Finish up functionality for importing passwords from files
* Fix create backup phrase for desktop OS's, so now the backup phrase is automatically written to the selected file
* Remove CHANGELOG.md from .gitignore

## 1.0.0 (29 July 2026)
* Fix layout so content is now centered
* Remove duplicate definition of home widgets
* Work on trying to get background server to start

## 1.0.0 (30 July 2026)
* Add send data functionality
* Start working on connection refused error handling

## 1.0.0 (31 July 2026)
* Switch messages from server to app from strings to dictionaries
* Add error handling for connection errors

## 1.0.0 (08 August 2026)
* Work on receiving device deoffset data functionality
* Add new function to utilities to help with deoffseting offset strings
* Fix usernames, passwords, keys, and ivs not being reset between username offset

## 1.0.0 (18 August 2026)
* Add command to manually trigger offset and deoffset functions

## 1.0.0 (19 August 2026)
* Work on move offset function to offset string instead of offset user data
* Add missing comma between '-' and '!' characters
* Get receiving data functionality mostly working
* Fix app crashing on Ubuntu

## 1.0.0 (26 August 2026)
* Fix data migration so if service and username already exists on receiving device, existing password will be overwritten
* Got data migration working from pypass to bastion pass except on android

## 1.0.0 (27 August 2026)
* Fix bug causing legacy data transfer to fail when no data already saved on receiving device
* Fix bug preventing already existing services/usernames to be overwritten in data transfer
* Fix saved legacy received data to wrong file
* Add file cleanup after receiving data

## 1.0.0 (28 August 2026)
* Fix offset_user_data not being reset after data transfer, preventing multiple data transfer between app start from working
* Cleanup print statements in utils.py

## 1.0.0 (29 August 2026)
* Add data offset parameter to offset_string when offset_number is equal to zero
* Delete debug_server.py and migration_server.py as they are no longer needed
* Cleanup background_server.py file

## 1.0.0 (30 August 2026)
* Fix message listener crashing after dialog pops up on mac

## 1.0.0 (31 August 2026)
* Update import_from_file utility to use read().split("\n") instead of readlines()
* Update test suite and add new tests for new utilities

## 1.0.0 (1 September 2026)
* Add secretstorge and jeepney to linux requirements in hopes of getting keyring to work on fedora
* Upgrade version of libgirepository from 1.0 to 2.0 in github CI and pyproject.toml
* Add separate package index for cryptography python3.13 - python3.15
* Update github CI to use `bastionpass` directory instead of `pypass`
* Move comma up so it isn't apart of the comment anymore
* Replace double quotes with single quotes in github CI
* Add step to github CI to sign android app on release
* Update OS verison of Ubuntu and Fedora in github CI
* Remove no longer needed argument for test suite
* Fix github CI failing when signing android app
* Update python version in CI to python3.14
* Add step that lists available keyrings
* Fix some typos in pyproject.toml file
* Remove random 'i' from pyproject.toml
* Add missing commas to pyproject.toml
* Force github CI to use node 24

## 1.0.0 (2 September 2026)
* Remove secretstorage from app requirements, as keyring automattically installs it

## 1.0.0 (6 September 2026)
* Add packages to system requirements to debian to ensure keyring works in minimized ubuntu
* Remove dbus from python requirements and add it to system package requirements
* If no keyring is found on linux, start the keyring service

## 1.0.0 (07 September 2026)
* Consolidate cryptography requirement declaration down to one declaration, and add extra package index to android install
* Switch from netifaces to netifaces-plus

## 1.0.0 (10 September 2026)
* Add custom package index to installer args for all platforms, not just android

## 1.0.0 (11 September 2026)
* Change github CI version from python3.14 to python3.13
